# Line endings: LF in the repo and in the working tree.
#
# Adopted 2026-11-26. Every text file was already LF in git; 17 of the 19 were CRLF in
# the working tree only because core.autocrlf=true converted them on checkout. So what a
# file looked like on disk depended on each machine's git config, and nothing here said
# which ending was intended.
#
# LF because that is what the Write tool and heredocs produce, and what the GitHub
# Actions (ubuntu) write into stats.json and videos.json. With eol=lf a CRLF write no
# longer shows as a diff and is committed as LF, whatever core.autocrlf says.
# .vscode/settings.json sets files.eol so the editor creates new files the same way.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Never let the text heuristic touch these.
*.jpg binary
*.png binary
*.mp4 binary
